  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0031","literal","Descending to the Warring States, extravagance and usurpation blazed hotter; they cut away the ritual canopies, probably hating words that harmed themselves.","Descending to the Warring States, extravagance and usurpation blazed hotter; they cut away the ritual registers, probably hating words that harmed themselves.","Chinese 削滅禮籍 means they destroyed the ritual registers/codices; 籍 is registers or written records, not canopies, and the proposed literal matches that sense.","high","applied"],
    ["s0110","idiomatic","When Qin swallowed the rival kingdoms it seized their court trains, which is why the Han “great progress” runs eighty-one follow-cars while the statutory halving uses thirty-six.","When Qin swallowed the rival kingdoms it seized their court trains, which is why the great equipage has eighty-one attendant chariots, while the statutory equipage is half that.","Chinese 故大駕屬車八十一乘，法駕半之 names neither Han nor thirty-six; the proposal removes those inventions and renders 大駕/法駕半之 as great equipage and statutory equipage half that.","high","applied"]
